Licensing
=========

forksync is dual-licensed under the MIT License and the Apache License 2.0.
You may use it under the terms of either license.

Every source file in this repository carries the header

    SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0

and there is no split in the code: unlike `rgx` and `posix7`, forksync has no
Apache-2.0-only subsystem, so the SPDX header is the same on every file and
the split is not something a reader has to reconstruct from a file list.

The MIT and Apache-2.0 option
-----------------------------

You may use this software under the terms of the MIT License, or under the
terms of the Apache License 2.0, at your option.

Apache-2.0 was chosen as the license this project intends for commercial
deployment: it carries an express patent grant and an explicit limitation of
liability, which a tool that rewrites your own GitHub repositories is better
off having. The MIT option remains available to anyone who prefers its terms,
and nothing here requires you to take the Apache-2.0 option.

